orgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px"><span>Markets up. Markets down. Markets up =E2=
=80=A6=3F</span></h2><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:=
#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">So, Joe. We=E2=80=99v=
e seen some serious volatility in the stock market after the midterms. Firs=
t markets rallied, then they had their worst day in nearly two years. This =
week, as Nvidia stock plunged because of the Jensen Huang affair, the rest =
of the market bounced back.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px geo=
rgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">What=
=E2=80=99s going on, and how much of all this is down to politics=3F</span>=
</p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 1=
5px"><span>Certainly some of it is down to politics. The initial rally afte=
r the midterms came in part from investors who had parked their cash on the=
 sidelines, in case of some unexpected event =E2=80=94 say, a contested ele=
ction. They bought back in when it became evident we were going to get a cl=
ear outcome.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;colo=
r:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The plunge the next day, though, came after s=
ome weaker than expected financial reports from a couple of A.I. companies,=
 and after investors began processing what Democratic control of Congress a=
nd some Democratic wins at the state level might actually mean for the A.I.=
 industry.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:=
#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But markets have rallied since and now seem to =
be trying to find some equilibrium. I haven=E2=80=99t yet spoken to any pro=
fessional investor who thinks we=E2=80=99re at the start of a more severe d=
ownturn. It=E2=80=99s more that perhaps the first leg of A.I. development, =
characterized by astronomical growth (and stock returns), may be slowing.</=
span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:=
0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">What are investors worried about=
=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>Many people were </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.=
com/f/newsletter/anlhGd6S_7slzB9cOGZCzg~~/AAAAARA~/4NJhtiZE44_BCC7Hu15zbdP6=
yzpN2cE8yUq12F23i0MaGfSz9NdalaKgyIust82xa36omWN41R_ayGdrXIn82EZ7BWCims7FCwL=
s3vyHMKkoc5fyUJ1X7sJPsJg55BCOSctiuxljx06DC12VRfXT0pMPY4EFKuvxxxFlM02ABZcipr=
uZNXR6jsNOT_VDAiAMRMTQa5ps_RfzhkAHomtTbJccp7YnDHZDTYsQJTvuQ6cUrvTG1CtpNXZ03=
iSHgVBk1BD7ijwEKEDuA-W-DI5UQ82a4RZUI2n7KfamXw7wbr_I3C-WktkP_xvSvAU6w8ac3cU6=
E94sdpzb4y9bp-_77ZqtaSmEXcLeuaQRT_LjpvIm7xZCZ0Od9_91hoY5jvAs" class=3D"css-=
sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decor=
ation:underline">already worried</a><span> about the rapid growth in A.I. s=
lowing down ahead of the midterms, and whether the huge amount of spending =
by A.I. companies would result in big profits any time soon.</span></p><p s=
tyle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><sp=
an>Then the midterms hit, and it wasn=E2=80=99t just that Democrats won con=
trol of Congress. They won governorships in states that are important hubs =
for data centers, sometimes by running anti-data-center campaigns. And sudd=
enly people really began to wonder if the rosy assumptions embedded in such=
 lofty stock prices were still reasonable, or whether prices needed to come=
 down a bit.</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D=
"0" style=3D"width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style=3D"text-align:center"><img wi=
